From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: requireAdministrator inside a manifest comment does not count

0259's scan of a program's manifest for requestedExecutionLevel matched one
inside an XML comment: HandBrake's manifest has the level it does not use
commented out before the one it does, and it asked for an administrator
every start. Comments are skipped.
---
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
@@ -744,6 +744,15 @@
         /* level="requireAdministrator" inside <requestedExecutionLevel ...> */
         for (i = 0; i < len && !ret; i++)
         {
+            /* not inside a comment: HandBrake's manifest has the level it
+             * does not use, commented out, before the one it does */
+            if (xml[i] == '<' && len - i >= 4 && !memcmp( xml + i, "<!--", 4 ))
+            {
+                for (i += 4; i + 3 <= len && memcmp( xml + i, "-->", 3 ); i++);
+                i += 2;
+                in_tag = FALSE;
+                continue;
+            }
             if (xml[i] == '<') in_tag = FALSE;
             if (!in_tag && len - i >= sizeof(tag) - 1)
             {
